**********************************************************************************************************************************************************************
													Steps for Silent Installation of 19c on RHEL with ASM
**********************************************************************************************************************************************************************

1. Create OS groups using the command below. Enter these commands as the 'root' user:

(a). Create OS groups
/usr/sbin/groupadd -g 501 oinstall
/usr/sbin/groupadd -g 502 dba
/usr/sbin/groupadd -g 503 asmdba
/usr/sbin/groupadd -g 504 asmoper
/usr/sbin/groupadd -g 506 asmadmin

(b). Create the users that will own the Oracle software using the commands as the 'root' user:

mkdir  /u01
/usr/sbin/useradd -u 501 -g oinstall -G dba oracle
chown -R oracle:oinstall /u01
usermod  -G asmdba,asmoper,asmadmin,dba,oinstall oracle
usermod -aG wheel oracle # This one we need when running cluster verification script with sudo
id oracle

#Change the password of oracle user
passwd oracle

(c) Create the Oracle Inventory Directory as 'oracle' user

mkdir -p /u01/app/oraInventory
chown -R oracle:oinstall /u01/app/oraInventory
chmod -R 775 /u01/app/oraInventory

(d) Creating the Oracle Grid Infrastructure Base and  Home Directory as 'oracle' user

mkdir -p /u01/app/19.3.0/db
mkdir -p /u01/app/19.3.0/grid
chown -R oracle:oinstall /u01/app/19.3.0/db
chown -R oracle:oinstall /u01/app/
chmod -R 775 /u01/app/19.3.0/grid

(e) Creating Oracle Software directory

mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software
chown -R oracle:oinstall /u01/app/oracle/software


